% Overlay rule file, passed to nmo alongside sssom-chain.rls.
%
% Its only purpose is to emit the traced predicate in a strictly line-oriented
% format. N-Triples writes exactly one `<s> <p> <o> .` per line, which is what
% makes `split -n l/K` a valid way to cut the fact list into contiguous ranges.
% The verbatim program's own `turtle` export is kept, but Turtle serializers may
% group statements by subject with `;` continuations, so it is not safe to parse
% line by line.
%
% Nothing here participates in inference: no rule, no import. Keeping it in a
% separate file is what lets sssom-chain.rls stay byte-identical to the program
% reported in knowsys/nemo#763.

@export inferredMapping :- ntriples{resource = $factsfile} .
